8,4,10,11,12,13,14,15,16,17,19,20,22,23,26,27],"holds":[{"raw":"ר' בנימין ב\"ח, רב חיננא ב\"ח, רב יוסף ב\"ח, ר' יצחק ב\"ח, לוי ב\"ח, מנימן ב\"ח","reason":"Binyamin and Minyamin have separate received slots and adjacent cross-references. The underlying exact primary referent for Minyamin remains open.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 764:1","target":{"entry":764,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2507:1","target":{"entry":2507,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"raw":"ובשס\"ח נשתנה הגירסא ונכתב בצדו","reason":"The exact Bavli and Rosh have the Ashi/Rav alternative, and Rif has bar Abba/Rav. The particular edition behind the gloss and the separately reported bare Chiyya/Yochanan version remain to collate.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 113a:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_113a.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rosh on Shabbat 15:1:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rosh_on_Shabbat_15.1.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Rif Shabbat 41b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rif_Shabbat_41b.8"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"raw":"זבחים (כ\"ה ב') א\"ר חייא (בר אבא) א\"ר יוחנן","reason":"The first teaching has bare Chiyya. The checked continuation uses bar Abba in address and then in a separate Yochanan teaching. Preserve the gloss proposal.","evidence":[{"reference":"Zevachim 25b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_25b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Zevachim 25b:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_25b.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Zevachim 25b:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_25b.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"קרוב בעיני שצ\"ל רב חייא בר אדא","reason":"The conjecture has a precise parallel. Ketubot 8b names bar Abba and has variants about the son or children and the teaching, while 111b names Adda. Retain the difference.","evidence":[{"reference":"Ketubot 8b:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_8b.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Ketubot 111b:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_111b.20"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"רבי חייא בר אשי ובכ\"מ רב חייא","reason":"The cited line confirms Rabbi. The gloss’s general statement about title distribution remains a report.","evidence":[{"reference":"Berakhot 42a:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_42a.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"צ\"ל בר יוסף ול\"ת","reason":"The checked Pesachim and Bekhorot read Yosef. Bava Metzia gives a different local chain, with Rabbi Elai citing Chiyya son of Rabbi Yosi. Keep the gloss’s emendation and the three checked texts visible.","evidence":[{"reference":"Pesachim 7a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_7a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bekhorot 39a:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot_39a.20"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Metzia 117a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_117a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"נ\"ל שצ\"ל חיננא ל\"ת","reason":"The exact Niddah retains Chiyya. The separate Chinena entry motivates the proposal.","evidence":[{"reference":"Niddah 45a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_45a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1434:1","target":{"entry":1434,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"raw":"אולי צ\"ל אמי ל\"ת","reason":"The Gittin and Shabbat parallels differ exactly as the gloss reports. Preserve Assi and Ammi as separate witness forms.","evid